description:
Goal
Finish the work that was intentionally left outside fz-bin after protocol dispatch itself landed.

Signal
The fz-bin epic closed the unresolved multi-target protocol callsite failure. Remaining work is narrower:
- native indirect closure calls still need a real multi-surface callable boundary instead of the deterministic fallback left by fz-bin.18;
- shared Enum.reduce/3 bridge captures still need generic direct-callable shape correlation;
- struct-vs-map dispatch still needs a nominal-tag test before structural map projection;
- enum_map_family still exposes a native direct-closure fast-path arity mismatch.

Strategy
Keep these independent. Each child owns one current failure mode and must retire any temporary fixture defers or native fallback it makes obsolete. Do not re-open the old fz-bin multi-target dispatch problem statement; that class is closed.
